o we can apply the above formula. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062142/assets/11376e6ef18b151a6dd1a02dd09f20b72bce3160c718f4095b4f08b23721ff1f.png)\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t}{2},\\,y=\\frac{1}{2t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =4, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2t})=-\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}(4)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}})-(2)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}-1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{t}-t){|}_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)-(4-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342866 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342867 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342868 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342869 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342870 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1041 "selection" 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342867 13194139535303 true] [17592186342865 1110 #uuid "e635918e-30da-5590-8a31-9f0712131189" 13194139535303 true] [17592186342866 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535303 true] [17592186342866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535303 true] [175